# Idea: "Mood Palette" – A Visual Mood Tracker and Color Diary

**Concept:**  
"Mood Palette" is an innovative, compact Tkinter app that lets users log their daily mood visually by selecting a color from a professional palette. Over time, the app builds a calendar-like grid of colored squares—each representing the user's mood for that day. Users can add short notes to each entry and review patterns in their emotional well-being through color trends.

This idea combines visual journaling with emotional awareness, offering an intuitive interface for self-reflection—something not commonly found in simple Tkinter apps.

---

## Code: Mood Palette App

```python
import tkinter as tk
from tkinter import ttk, messagebox, simpledialog
from datetime import date
import calendar

# Professional palette (calm & modern)
MOOD_COLORS = [
    ("Calm", "#6EC6CA"),
    ("Happy", "#FFD166"),
    ("Energetic", "#EF476F"),
    ("Focused", "#26547C"),
    ("Anxious", "#FF8C42"),
    ("Sad", "#4B3F72")
]

FONT_TITLE = ('Segoe UI', 18, 'bold')
FONT_LABEL = ('Segoe UI', 12)
FONT_NOTE = ('Segoe UI', 10)

class MoodPaletteApp(tk.Tk):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        self.title("Mood Palette - Visual Mood Tracker")
        self.configure(bg="#f7f7fa")
        self.resizable(False, False)
        
        # Storage for moods (date: (color_name, note))
        self.mood_log = {}
        
        # Layout frames
        header_frame = tk.Frame(self, bg="#22223b")
        header_frame.pack(fill='x')
        
        title_lbl = tk.Label(header_frame,
                             text="Mood Palette",
                             font=FONT_TITLE,
                             fg="#fff",
                             bg="#22223b",
                             pady=10)
        title_lbl.pack()
        
        main_frame = tk.Frame(self, bg="#f7f7fa")
        main_frame.pack(padx=20,pady=(5,15))
        
        # Today's mood selector
        today_box = ttk.LabelFrame(main_frame,text="Today's Mood:", labelanchor='n')
        today_box.grid(row=0,column=0,pady=(0,10),sticky='ew')
        
        self.selected_mood_idx=tk.IntVar(value=-1)
        
        for idx,(name,color) in enumerate(MOOD_COLORS):
            btn=tk.Radiobutton(today_box,text=name,bg=color,value=idx,
                               variable=self.selected_mood_idx,font=FONT_LABEL,
                               indicatoron=False,width=11,height=2,
                               selectcolor=color,tristatevalue=-1,
                               relief='groove',bd=2,cursor="hand2",
                               activebackground=color)
            btn.grid(row=0,column=idx,padx=(3 if idx else 8),pady=(5),sticky='ew')
```

